tion systems; cryogenic equipment, such as trailers and mobile storage equipment for the distribution of liquified hydrogen, oxygen, argon, nitrogen, and other cryogenic gases; GenSure, a stationary fuel cell solution; and liquid hydrogen. The company serves customers in material handling operations, fuel cell electric vehicle fleets, and stationary power applications through its direct sales force, original equipment manufacturers, and dealer networks. Plug Power Inc. was incorporated in 1997 and is based in Slingerlands, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jose Luis Crespo | CEO, President & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2022)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $303K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 26%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $22K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Plug Power, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.6B market cap on $710M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years and +21% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at -81% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and -24% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $647M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -22.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 20.8% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 4.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-5.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (22.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Industrials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 216% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 71/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Industrials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 153% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why Did NVDA, ALT, PLUG Stocks Plunge To 52-Week Lows Today?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/why-did-nvda-alt-plug-034434129.html","date":"2026-11-13","ti